# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/002_loops_while_do_for.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 002_loops_while_do_for
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = All three loop forms at their zero-iteration and single-iteration boundaries, omitted for-clauses, continue, and nested break and continue, with every bound read from volatile storage
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every loop bound is a small non-negative literal staged through the volatile int
vlimit, so every loop terminates and no trip count can be negative. The largest
accumulated value anywhere is 55, so no signed overflow is possible on any plain
int. The for(;;) loop is exited by an unconditional break once count reaches 4,
so it cannot run away. There is no shift, no pointer arithmetic and no division;
the only remainder operations are i % 2 and i % 3 on non-negative i, so the
divisor is never zero and the dividend is never negative. Every object is
written before it is read: vlimit is assigned before each read, n, sum, count, i
and the block-scoped j and k are all assigned before use. No object is modified
twice between sequence points; each volatile write and each volatile read stands
in its own statement or its own controlling expression. There is no aliasing, no
address is taken, no uninitialised storage is read, and nothing depends on
padding bytes or on the relative addresses of unrelated objects. No evaluation
order is relied upon: no printf argument list contains a side effect.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is printed. Plain char is never used as a value,
which matters because char signedness was measured to differ across the four
targets: signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. Every
printed value has type int, which is 32 bits on all four targets, so no value
depends on the measured pointer and long width difference (4 bytes on i686,
8 bytes on the other three). No address, no pointer value, no sizeof result and
no floating-point value is printed. The loop counters are all small so no result
approaches any width boundary. All 12 cells are therefore expected to produce
byte-identical stdout, and no target restriction is needed.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
while_zero=0
while_one=1
while_sum=55
do_while_false_cond=1
do_while_one=1
do_while_squares=55
for_zero=0 i_after=0
for_one=1 i_after=1
for_forever_break=4
for_no_increment=6
for_continue_even_sum=20
while_continue_sum=37
nested_break=8 outer_iterations=4
nested_continue=12
for_do_while_mix=6
for_countdown_zero=0
for_countdown_three=3
END
